From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:03:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/win32, nvk: D3D11 and D3D12 swap chains through the
 enhanced composed present

D3D presents in a Helios guest go through DXGI, the Helios UMDs and the
KMD, never through a Vulkan swapchain.  Where a Helios D3D driver runs on
this NVK and enhancement is on for the process, NVK hooks DXGI's
IDXGIFactory::CreateSwapChain and IDXGIFactory2::CreateSwapChainForHwnd
(after the UMD's FlipUpgrade hooks, which chains not taken still go
through) and gives the application a swap chain of its own
(IDXGISwapChain4):

  - its back buffers are textures of the application's size on its
    device; Present copies the current one into a ring of three shared
    textures on the application's queue (D3D11: CopyResource and an event
    query, the immediate context made multithread-protected; D3D12: a
    command list and a fence) and returns;
  - a thread per swap chain waits for the copy, runs the enhancement
    passes on an NVK device of its own in the process (the ring textures
    imported by their Helios resource ids, KMT handles for D3D11, NT
    handles for D3D12) into output slots of the window's size, and presents
    them paced through the composed present's D3D11 device and DXGI flip
    swap chain on the window.

ResizeBuffers rebuilds everything at the new size; exclusive fullscreen
is not entered (SetFullscreenState is recorded, the window stays as it
is).  Formats other than 8-bit BGRA/RGBA and multisampled chains go to
DXGI as before.  MESA_WSI_ENHANCE_D3D=0 or EnhanceD3D=0 leaves D3D
swap chains alone; with enhancement off nothing is hooked.
